can click on and see the website.
你可以点进去看那个网站。

766
00:30:21.600 --> 00:30:24.040
And it's, it's really insane.
这真的，真的太疯狂了。

767
00:30:24.560 --> 00:30:29.140
Carter wrote and recorded an absolutely insane song in French in the perspective.
卡尔以某种视角用法语写并录制了一首绝对疯狂的歌。

768
00:30:29.280 --> 00:30:30.280
It's this French couple.
这是一对法国夫妇。

769
00:30:30.500 --> 00:30:31.640
It's a French man.
是一个法国男人。

770
00:30:31.800 --> 00:30:32.620
This connects back.
这又联系起来了。

771
00:30:32.720 --> 00:30:34.020
It all connects back to Guillaume somehow.
不知怎么的，这一切又和纪尧姆联系起来了。

772
00:30:34.260 --> 00:30:35.260
Back to Guillaume.
又回到了纪尧姆。

773
00:30:35.640 --> 00:30:38.620
I don't think Guillaume has this specific fetish with his wife.
我觉得纪尧姆对他的妻子应该没有这种特殊的癖好。

774
00:30:38.780 --> 00:30:42.100
I hope I have no judgment if so, but it's a French guy.
如果有的话我希望我没有评判的意思，但这是一个法国男人。

775
00:30:42.100 --> 00:30:44.260
And his wife dressing in a garbage bag.
和他的妻子穿着垃圾袋。

776
00:30:44.660 --> 00:30:47.320
And it's just, you see them throughout their day in this series of photos.
然后就是，在这一系列照片里你能看到他们一天的生活。

777
00:30:47.320 --> 00:30:48.700
They're like walking down the street.
他们走在街上。

778
00:30:48.900 --> 00:30:49.980
They're trying to hail a cab.
他们在试图拦出租车。

779
00:30:50.160 --> 00:30:53.180
And she's in a garbage bag and he looks very French.
而她穿着一个垃圾袋，他看起来非常法国。

780
00:30:53.560 --> 00:30:54.720
And it's absolutely insane.
这简直太疯狂了。

781
00:30:54.860 --> 00:30:59.060
And Carter wrote a song that's Carter and Wendy the waitress, Charlene Amoya.
然后卡尔写了一首歌，由卡尔和女服务员温迪（查琳·阿莫亚饰）合唱。

782
00:30:59.500 --> 00:31:03.320
She sang the female part of the song and Carter sang the male part in French.
她唱了歌里的女声部分，卡尔用法语唱了男声部分。

783
00:31:03.500 --> 00:31:06.280
And that's playing on the website as this photo montage happens.
随着照片蒙太奇的播放，这首歌也同时在网站上播放。

784
00:31:06.280 --> 00:31:07.320
I've seen this couple.
我见过这对夫妇。

785
00:31:07.780 --> 00:31:11.100
And it was just shot around the Fox lot, but I guess try to look like France or something.
这只是在福克斯制片厂周围拍的，但我想是尽量拍得像法国或者别的什么地方。

786
00:31:11.100 --> 00:31:13.300
It's not high production value, I would say.
可以说，这没什么制作成本。

787
00:31:13.460 --> 00:31:15.300
But it's fucking insane.
但它他妈的太疯狂了。

788
00:31:15.660 --> 00:31:16.980
And it is worth looking at.
而且非常值得一看。

789
00:31:17.140 --> 00:31:18.860
It's really, talk about fever dream.
真的是，简直就像是一场狂热的梦。

790
00:31:19.060 --> 00:31:21.460
Everything about these episodes was a fever dream.
这些剧集的方方面面都像是一场狂热的梦。

791
00:31:21.700 --> 00:31:30.180
And this old man, he must admit he fell in love with you in New York City.
而这位老人，他必须承认他在纽约市爱上了你。

792
00:31:30.960 --> 00:31:33.200
And now, commercials.
现在是广告时间。

793
00:31:40.720 --> 00:31:41.660
End of commercials.
广告结束。

794
00:31:42.000 --> 00:31:42.880
Back to show.
回到节目。

795
00:31:45.790 --> 00:31:48.550
So, also though, explain what happened.
所以，不过，还是解释一下发生了什么。

796
00:31:48.690 --> 00:31:51.710
So, Lily wants to sell her paintings.
所以，莉莉想卖掉她的画。

797
00:31:51.970 --> 00:31:57.390
Yeah, Lily says, well, I shouldn't have to sell my great clothes because what will I wear?
对，莉莉说，好吧，我不应该卖掉我那些漂亮的衣服，因为我以后穿什么？

798
00:31:57.490 --> 00:31:59.990
We should just sell my amazing paintings and that will make the money.
我们应该卖掉我那些惊艳的画作，这样就能赚到钱了。

799
00:32:00.110 --> 00:32:05.290
And Marshall, without thinking, says, no, but these aren't real paintings.
而马歇尔想都没想就说，不，但这些又不是真正的画。

800
00:32:05.290 --> 00:32:07.070
You're not going to sell these for thousands of dollars.
你不可能靠这些卖出几千美元。

801
00:32:07.250 --> 00:32:08.890
And she is really devastated.
她真的深受打击。

802
00:32:09.130 --> 00:32:11.910
He says it in a way that makes her feel he doesn't believe in her.
他说这句话的方式让她觉得他不信任她。

803
00:32:11.910 --> 00:32:14.890
I like the kind of the couple issue that comes out of that.
我喜欢由此引发的那种伴侣之间的问题。

804
00:32:15.030 --> 00:32:16.470
I think it's a good meaty issue.
我觉得这是一个很有分量的好问题。

805
00:32:16.570 --> 00:32:18.910
And I think that could have been the whole episode.
而且我觉得这完全可以撑起整集。

806
00:32:19.150 --> 00:32:20.770
And it couldn't, all these other bells and whistles.
但不行，还有所有这些花里胡哨的东西。

807
00:32:20.910 --> 00:32:28.350
If we were not in a nine episode, 11 week fever dream, we may have made that more the theme and put everyone more on that maybe.
如果我们不是身处那种只有九集、却要播十一周的狂热梦境中，我们可能会把这作为更多的主题，也许会让所有人都更多地聚焦于此。

808
00:32:28.950 --> 00:32:31.170
But that's the actual beating heart.
但那是真正跳动的心脏。

809
00:32:31.170 --> 00:32:33.550
If there is one in this episode, it's like, that's real.
如果这一集里有的话，那就感觉，那是真实的。

810
00:32:33.710 --> 00:32:34.690
That's a real couple issue.
那是真正的伴侣问题。

811
00:32:35.110 --> 00:32:36.210
Do you believe in me?
你相信我吗？

812
00:32:36.610 --> 00:32:37.570
You're my life partner.
你是我的生活伴侣。

813
00:32:37.770 --> 00:32:38.590
Do you believe in me?
你相信我吗？

814
00:32:38.750 --> 00:32:40.330
That's the real thing in this episode.
这才是这一集里最真实的东西。

815
00:32:40.330 --> 00:32:44.450
It also is like, what are you asking of your partner when you're an artist?
这也是在探讨，当你成为一名艺术家时，你对伴侣的要求是什么？

816
00:32:44.650 --> 00:32:51.490
Which is, you know, you've talked about, Greg, like in the original, like watching Rebecca watch How I Met Your Mother was how you watched How I Met Your Mother.
也就是，你知道的，格雷格，你之前谈过的，就像在原版里那样，看丽贝卡看《老爸老妈浪漫史》的过程，就是你看《老爸老妈浪漫史》的方式。

817
00:32:51.590 --> 00:32:52.210
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

818
00:32:52.750 --> 00:32:54.870
Which is extraordinarily unpleasant for her.
这对她来说极其痛苦。

819
00:32:55.270 --> 00:32:56.390
Why didn't you laugh at that?
你为什么不笑？

820
00:32:56.430 --> 00:32:57.010
It was a good line.
那句台词写得很好。

821
00:32:57.150 --> 00:32:57.670
You didn't hear it?
你没听到吗？

822
00:32:57.770 --> 00:32:58.510
The sound makes us off?
是音效让我们不在状态吗？

823
00:32:58.810 --> 00:32:59.130
Yeah.
对。

824
00:32:59.130 --> 00:33:11.710
But, you know, what we want from our loved ones, from our parents, from our spouses, when we make something, it's a really delicate thing, how to talk to us.
但是，你知道的，当我们创作作品时，我们从爱人、父母、配偶那里所期望的，如何跟我们交流，这是一件非常微妙的事情。

825
00:33:11.710 --> 00:33:15.350
Like, I had to train my parents after seeing plays.
比如，看完话剧后，我得训练我的父母。

826
00:33:15.630 --> 00:33:15.990
Yeah.
对。

827
00:33:16.090 --> 00:33:21.990
I would say, you can say the set was great, but not the first thing you say to me.
我会说，你们可以说布景很棒，但别把它当成对我说第一句话。

828
00:33:24.610 --> 00:33:29.670
You're welcome to say it and feel it, but it can't be the first thing you say.
你们完全可以这么说、这么觉得，但不能一开口就说这个。

829
00:33:30.010 --> 00:33:31.110
This is years ago.
那是好几年前的事了。

830
00:33:31.110 --> 00:33:31.870
They've gotten better.
他们现在好多了。

831
00:33:32.170 --> 00:33:33.770
But, yeah.
不过，对。

832
00:33:34.410 --> 00:33:37.870
I can say the red cowboy boots were great, but don't start there.
我可以接受说红色的牛仔靴很棒，但别从那开始说。

833
00:33:39.710 --> 00:33:41.650
About my whole work on the series.
关于我在这部剧里的全部工作。

834
00:33:43.050 --> 00:33:47.490
There were two notable guest stars, I think, that I want to shout out on this episode.
我想在这一集里特别鸣谢两位重要的客串明星。

835
00:33:48.410 --> 00:33:49.250
Larry Wilmore.
拉里·威尔莫尔。

836
00:33:49.550 --> 00:33:49.830
Yep.
对。

837
00:33:50.790 --> 00:33:52.050
From The Daily Show.
来自《每日秀》。

838
00:33:52.390 --> 00:33:53.630
Yeah, Larry Wilmore, the great Larry Wilmore.
对，拉里·威尔莫尔，伟大的拉里·威尔莫尔。

839
00:33:53.830 --> 00:33:57.270
Yeah, I mean, iconic, you know, writer, performer.
对，我的意思是，标志性的，你知道的，编剧、表演者。

840
00:33:57.590 --> 00:33:58.890
He went on to have his own show.
他后来有了自己的节目。

841
00:33:58.910 --> 00:34:02.430
He created The Bernie Mac Show, and he had his own show after The Daily Show for years.
他创作了《伯尼·麦克秀》，在离开《每日秀》后，他做自己的节目好多年。

842
00:34:02.510 --> 00:34:03.190
Really funny dude.
真的是个很有趣的家伙。

843
00:34:03.190 --> 00:34:08.210
And he was the veterinarian in this who discovered that Lily's paintings are hypnotic to dogs.
他就是这一集里的兽医，发现了莉莉的画对狗有催眠作用。

844
00:34:08.430 --> 00:34:08.790
Yeah.
对。

845
00:34:08.830 --> 00:34:10.130
Which was a twist I liked.
这个反转我很喜欢。

846
00:34:10.190 --> 00:34:11.570
I liked the weirdness of...
我喜欢那种奇特感……

847
00:34:11.570 --> 00:34:12.350
I like it, too.
我也喜欢。

848
00:34:12.450 --> 00:34:12.790
Also, it's success.
而且，这也是成功。

849
00:34:12.930 --> 00:34:15.130
Her art has success, but just with dogs.
她的艺术成功了，只不过对象是狗。

850
00:34:15.290 --> 00:34:16.210
In the canine kingdom.
在犬类王国里。

851
00:34:16.410 --> 00:34:16.490
Yeah.
是啊。

852
00:34:16.630 --> 00:34:16.730
Yeah.
对。

853
00:34:17.210 --> 00:34:21.490
No, that was a really charming thing where it was like, these are valuable.
不，那是一种非常迷人的做法，就好像在说，这些都是很有价值的。

854
00:34:22.010 --> 00:34:24.070
Yes, there is a value to this art.
没错，这种艺术是有价值的。

855
00:34:24.490 --> 00:34:24.890
Right.
对。

856
00:34:24.910 --> 00:34:25.330
It does.
确实如此。

857
00:34:25.470 --> 00:34:26.310
It has an effect.
它有效果。

858
00:34:26.550 --> 00:34:27.390
That's the point of art.
这就是艺术的意义所在。

859
00:34:27.690 --> 00:34:28.950
It's to have a captivating effect.
就是要产生迷人的效果。

860
00:34:29.930 --> 00:34:31.110
Why judge the audience?
为什么要评判观众呢？

861
00:34:31.350 --> 00:34:32.670
If it's dogs, it's dogs.
如果是狗，那就是狗。

862
00:34:32.670 --> 00:34:34.010
At least somebody is into it.
至少有人喜欢。

863
00:34:34.830 --> 00:34:40.650
So also, I don't know if you know this, but the heroin addict who was next to...
另外，我不知道你知不知道，坐在旁边那个海洛因瘾君子……

864
00:34:40.650 --> 00:34:41.930
He is a improv legend.
他是一位即兴表演传奇人物。

865
00:34:42.250 --> 00:34:43.110
Matt Besser, right?
马特·贝瑟，对吧？

866
00:34:43.390 --> 00:34:43.910
Matt Besser.
马特·贝瑟。

867
00:34:44.090 --> 00:34:44.850
Yeah, really funny.
对，真的很好笑。

868
00:34:44.990 --> 00:34:47.190
We definitely should have used him more than we did.
我们绝对应该多用他一些，而不是现在这样。

869
00:34:47.510 --> 00:34:53.510
One of the founders with Amy Poehler and, you know, others of Upright Citizens Brigade.
他与埃米·波勒以及其他人是“アップライト・シチズンズ・ブリゲード”（Upright Citizens Brigade）的创始人之一。

870
00:34:53.910 --> 00:34:58.590
I got to say that I saw Matt Besser at UCB one night.
我得说，有一天晚上我在 UCB 见过马特·贝瑟。

871
00:34:58.730 --> 00:35:00.650
And I think Amy Poehler was there that night.
我想埃米·波勒那天也在。

872
00:35:00.730 --> 00:35:01.650
It was like they'd already...
感觉他们当时已经……

873
00:35:01.650 --> 00:35:03.890
He might have still been there, but Poehler had already gone.
他可能还在那儿，但波勒已经走了。

874
00:35:03.990 --> 00:35:07.850
She was kind of coming back to just like keep well-oiled, you know?
她回来大概只是为了保持状态，你懂的？

875
00:35:07.950 --> 00:35:08.150
Yeah.
对。

876
00:35:08.150 --> 00:35:15.810
And I saw Matt Besser do a sketch with another guy that was so impressive to me from an improv
我看到马特·贝瑟和另一个家伙表演了一个小品，从即兴表演的

877
00:35:15.810 --> 00:35:16.270
perspective.
角度来看，这让我印象深刻。

878
00:35:16.450 --> 00:35:16.570
Yeah.
对。

879
00:35:16.750 --> 00:35:19.390
It felt like watching...
感觉就像在看……

880
00:35:19.390 --> 00:35:22.230
He wasn't doing anything but listening.
他什么都没做，只是在倾听。

881
00:35:22.430 --> 00:35:24.170
He wasn't trying to make anyone laugh.
他并没有刻意去逗大家笑。

882
00:35:24.250 --> 00:35:26.290
He was just listening for the thing.
他只是在聆听那个契机。

883
00:35:26.450 --> 00:35:30.690
It felt like watching a surfer out, like let little waves go by.
感觉就像看着一个冲浪者，让小浪从身边滑过。

884
00:35:31.210 --> 00:35:31.430
Yeah.
对。

885
00:35:31.710 --> 00:35:32.670
Until the big...
直到大浪……

886
00:35:32.670 --> 00:35:33.630
Until the one came.
直到那个浪来临。

887
00:35:33.630 --> 00:35:34.290
Yes, yes.
对，对。

888
00:35:34.550 --> 00:35:35.830
And once he got the thing...
一旦他抓住了那个点……

889
00:35:35.830 --> 00:35:38.770
Which is very Jalen Brunsonian, too.
这也非常像杰伦·布伦森的风格。

890
00:35:38.970 --> 00:35:40.670
He waits for his moment.
他在等待自己的时刻。

891
00:35:40.790 --> 00:35:41.270
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

892
00:35:41.450 --> 00:35:41.830
Yes, yes.
对，对。

893
00:35:42.710 --> 00:35:44.150
I just saw him...
我刚看到他……

894
00:35:44.150 --> 00:35:47.250
Something clicked on in his eyes and then it was suddenly the funniest thing in the world.
他的眼中闪过一丝光芒，然后突然间这就成了世界上最好笑的事。

895
00:35:47.350 --> 00:35:47.550
Yeah.
对。

896
00:35:47.670 --> 00:35:51.610
But he risked being quite unfunny for quite a while.
但他冒着挺长一段时间都一点不好笑的风险。

897
00:35:51.790 --> 00:35:52.130
Yes.
是的。

898
00:35:52.610 --> 00:35:53.690
Until he got the thing.
直到他抓住了那个点。

899
00:35:53.950 --> 00:35:55.650
Risk is a good verb there.
“冒险”这个动词用得真好。

900
00:35:55.930 --> 00:35:57.690
It's the willingness to risk.
这就是勇于承担风险。

901
00:35:57.850 --> 00:35:57.990
Yeah.
是啊。

902
00:35:58.030 --> 00:35:58.510
It was amazing.
太棒了。

903
00:35:58.670 --> 00:35:59.030
I don't know.
我不知道。

904
00:35:59.170 --> 00:36:00.370
I think I met him on set.
我想我是在片场认识他的。

905
00:36:00.370 --> 00:36:01.990
But I always...
但我总是……

906
00:36:01.990 --> 00:36:06.070
Like just as an actor and appreciator of comedy and improv, I always remember that.
就好像作为一个演员、喜剧和即兴表演的欣赏者，我一直都记得那个。

907
00:36:06.230 --> 00:36:07.250
You know what you should have done?
你知道你本来应该怎么做吗？

908
00:36:07.250 --> 00:36:07.930
That's like a really great lesson.
这真是一个非常棒的教训。

909
00:36:08.090 --> 00:36:08.850
You should have done, Matt.
你本来应该那么做的，马特。

910
00:36:09.650 --> 00:36:12.050
Matt, how would you play this Red Cowboy Boots game?
马特，你会怎么玩这个“红色牛仔靴”游戏？

911
00:36:14.530 --> 00:36:15.930
You'd be like, I'd write something better.
你大概会觉得，我会写出更好的东西。

912
00:36:17.150 --> 00:36:19.010
You know what would be even more of a certain thing?
你知道什么才更像是板上钉钉的事吗？

913
00:36:19.110 --> 00:36:22.050
I'd think of something better in the moment without having written it.
我会当场想出更好的东西，而且不用提前写好。

914
00:36:22.510 --> 00:36:23.150
Improv something better.
